  "verbalization": "Simenepag isopropyl is shown to interact with Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein, which in turn is a target of multiple entities, including Npc187605 and Ertugliflozin, all of which ultimately target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. This suggests a potential pathway where Simenepag isopropyl may influence the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through its interaction with Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein. The evidence is supported by a series of target relationships, with varying confidence scores, indicating a possible but not definitive mechanistic link. The core mechanism appears to involve the modulation of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 via an intermediate protein, Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein, which is a plausible candidate for a regulatory or functional interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Simenepag isopropyl to exert its effects on UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a complex network of molecular interactions, though further validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the relationship.",
